# Expectation record for 03_initializers/006_designated_mixed_nested.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 006_designated_mixed_nested
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Mixed positional and designated initializers inside nested aggregates -- positional outer with designated inner, designated outer with an unlabelled inner brace, array-of-struct positional then designated, two-dimensional positional row then element designator, and two three-level struct mixtures including a combined index-and-member designator -- for static and automatic storage duration, every member read back individually; the OVERLAPPING-designator spelling is deliberately concentrated in this area's designated-array program rather than duplicated here, so that this translation unit needs no diagnostic-control directive at all, as impl_defined_notes records
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the precondition that
makes both differential oracles sound: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything at all, so a divergence over it would prove nothing about either one.

THERE IS NO READ OF UNINITIALIZED STORAGE, which needs stating first because most of the values
this program prints are ones its initializers never mention. Every object here has an initializer,
and C11 6.7.9p19 and p21 require members and elements not explicitly initialized to be initialized
implicitly as an object with static storage duration would be -- that is, to zero for the int
members used throughout. That holds for automatic duration exactly as for static, because an
aggregate with ANY initializer is fully initialized. This covers every zero printed by this
program, including g_pos_desig_in.in.p, the whole of g_arr_pos_then_desig[1], all of row 1 and
five of the six neighbours in row 2 of g_m_pos_then_desig, g_deep_mixed.pr[0], g_deep_desig.o.tag,
o.in.q and o.trailer, g_deep_desig.pr[1].p, and the corresponding members of the automatic twins.
Every one of those values is determinate rather than indeterminate, and that guarantee is the
feature under test rather than an assumption of the test's.

NO MEMBER OR ELEMENT RECEIVES TWO INITIALIZERS. Every designator in this program addresses a
member or element that no earlier initializer has set, and every positional initializer following
a designator lands on the NEXT subobject rather than on one already initialized, which C11
6.7.9p17 fixes. The result of each initializer is therefore fully determined by C11 6.7.9 and
there is no overriding initializer anywhere. The individual cases are:

  - g_pos_desig_in = { 1, { .q = 3 }, 4 }: positional 1 initializes tag; the braced block binds to
    the next member in and uses a designator inside it so only in.q is set and in.p remains
    implicitly zero; positional 4 then initializes trailer.
  - g_desig_pos_in = { .tag = 11, { .p = 12, .q = 13 }, 14 }: the designator sets tag, after which
    the current object advances so the unlabelled brace binds to in, and the trailing 14
    initializes trailer.
  - g_arr_pos_then_desig = { { 21, 22 }, [2] = { 25, 26 } }: element 0 positional, element 2
    designated, element 1 never named and therefore implicitly zero.
  - g_m_pos_then_desig = { { 1, 2, 3 }, [2][1] = 8 }: row 0 positional, then a designator naming a
    single element of row 2; row 1 and the remaining elements of row 2 are implicitly zero.
  - g_deep_mixed = { { 31, { .q = 33 }, 34 }, { [1] = { 37, 38 } } } and its automatic twin
    l_deep_mixed nest the first form inside a struct deep and add a designated element of the
    sibling array member, leaving the unnamed element of that array implicitly zero.
  - g_deep_desig = { .o = { .in.p = 42 }, .pr = { { 43, 44 }, [1].q = 46 } }: an outer member
    designator, a nested submember designator, a positional array element, and a combined
    index-and-member designator [1].q, none of which collide.
  - l_arr_mixed = { { 61, 62 }, [2].q = 66 }: a positional element followed by a combined
    index-and-member designator, so element 2's p stays zero while its q is set.

Order still matters even with no override present, and C11 6.7.9p19 fixes it by initializing in
initializer-list order: form 2's unlabelled brace has to bind to the member FOLLOWING the
designated one and its bare trailing value has to continue on past it. That is a separate rule
from the sequencing of an initializer list's side effects, which C11 6.7.9p23 leaves indeterminate.
Every initializer expression in this program is an integer constant expression with no side effect
at all, so there is nothing for 6.7.9p23 to make unspecified and the program's meaning does not
depend on the order in which side effects are sequenced.

EVERY DESIGNATOR INDEX IS IN RANGE: [2] within the [3] array of struct, [2][1] within the [3][3]
matrix, and [0] and [1] within the pr[2] array member. Every named member exists in the struct it
designates.

No arithmetic is performed on any initialized value, so signed overflow is impossible. The only
run-time arithmetic is on the loop counters i and j, each bounded strictly below its extent by a
literal equal to the declared one: i < 3 over the [3] arrays, i < 2 over pr[2], and i < 3 with
j < 3 over the [3][3] matrix. Every subscript is in bounds. The only pointers in the program are
therefore the ones subscripting derives: E[i] is defined as *(E + i), so each array subscript decays
its array to a pointer to that array's first element and adds an index the loop has already bounded
below the declared extent. Every such derived pointer consequently points at an element of the array
it was derived from, and is dereferenced only there; no one-past-end pointer is ever dereferenced, no
pointer arithmetic can leave the object it started in, no address is taken with the address-of
operator, no pointer is stored in an object, and none is printed. The only other pointer value in the
program is printf's format argument, which points into a string literal of static storage duration.

No shifts, no division, no remainder, no pointer casts and no cast of any kind appear in the file.
There is no aliasing violation: each object is read only through an lvalue of its own declared
type, which is int in every case, reached by member selection and subscripting only. Nothing is
modified twice between two sequence points. The initialized aggregates are never modified after
their initializers at all, so every value printed is the value its initializer gave it; the only
objects that are modified are the loop counters i and j, each assigned in the initial clause of its
own for statement and incremented in that statement's controlling expression, and each of those
assignments and increments is a full expression of its own, so each is separated from every other
access to the counter by a sequence point. Their bounds are the literals listed above, so neither
counter overflows. Each
printf call receives at most two loop counters and one int datum, none of which has a side effect,
so the unspecified order in which a call's arguments are evaluated cannot be observed. %d is the
only conversion specifier in the file and every corresponding argument has type int after the
default argument promotions, so no variadic argument is read at the wrong width. Every initializer
value is a small positive int, the largest being 76, so each is representable in int on every
supported target and no implicit conversion changes a value.

NO PADDING BYTE IS READ OR COMPARED. Only named members are accessed; no struct is printed as a
whole and no object representation is inspected. Padding contents are unspecified, so this is
essential to the soundness of the byte-exact comparison. All three struct types are composed
exclusively of int members and int-typed aggregates, so on every supported target they have no
internal padding in any case.

main returns a constant 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is
truncated by the operating system. Every input is a literal in this file: nothing is read from the
environment, the clock, the file system or the network, and iteration order is fixed by literal
bounds, so every cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.

No header is included anywhere and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`.
bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard
I/O header, so naming one would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a) while succeeding on the
reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by a compiler. This area is
granted no header exception; the corpus has exactly two, area 07's stdarg.h and the dedicated
bundled-header probe in area 12.

TWO AUTHORING CONSTRAINTS FROM THE MANDATED GATE, RECORDED SO THIS PROGRAM IS NOT "SIMPLIFIED"
INTO FAILURE BY A LATER CONTRIBUTOR:

  - Every nested aggregate is FULLY BRACED. The gate includes -Wall, which enables
    -Wmissing-braces, and -Werror promotes it to a hard error, so no brace may be elided from any
    initializer in this program.
  - Every struct initializer that omits a member does so through a DESIGNATOR, and every fully
    positional struct initializer supplies all of its members. Measurement with the reference
    compiler established that -Wmissing-field-initializers, enabled by -Wextra, does not fire for
    designated initializers in C but does fire for a positional partial struct such as
    `struct outer v = { 1 };`. No designator may therefore be removed from any initializer here.

This record declares no warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none, so no ub_audit_flags
override is used and both constraints above are satisfied by construction rather than by relaxing
the gate. The program is clean under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion
-Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror in the single native compile-only invocation the suite's warning
gate makes, with no diagnostic of any kind and no source-level diagnostic suppression anywhere in
the translation unit, and it builds and runs clean under the sanitizer gate
-fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are reference-compiler-only and
are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is untouched. One initializer
spelling is excluded to reach that clean audit rather than suppressed inside it, and the exclusion,
its measured reason and which of the harder forms remain under test are recorded in
impl_defined_notes below.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing that the harness reads: all four targets, all three optimization
levels and all three oracles are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, no gate
deviation is claimed under the ub_audit_flags key, and no implementation-defined value reaches
this program's output. One initializer SPELLING is nevertheless excluded from the source, and the
paragraph below states which, why, and which of the harder forms remain under test.

WHERE THE OVERLAPPING-DESIGNATOR SPELLING LIVES, AND WHY NOT HERE. Overriding a designated
initializer -- naming one subobject twice -- is well-defined C11 (6.7.9p19), and overriding at DEPTH
is worth testing separately from the flat form because the override has to interact correctly with
the current-object descent: an implementation that resolved designators against the wrong nesting
level would override a sibling, or the outer object, rather than the subobject named. That spelling
IS exercised in this area, in BOTH nesting directions, by the area's designated-array program:
004_designated_array.c carries g_over_row_elem, which names a whole row and then one element inside
it, and g_over_elem_row, which names the same element and then the same whole row. Those two contain
the identical initializers in opposite order, so they separate "last writer wins" from "any explicit
member survives" at depth -- element [0][1] must read 20 in the first and 2 in the second, and an
implementation holding the weaker rule would print 20 for both. The flat form, a struct-member
override and an automatic-duration override are carried there as well. So no coverage obligation is
outstanding, and this paragraph records a division of labour rather than a gap.

The reason it lives there rather than here is that the spelling cannot be written under the audit
gate untouched. GCC reports it under -Woverride-init, which -Wextra enables and which the gate's
-Werror makes fatal, and every override spelling MEASURED against that gate with the reference
compiler -- the flat and the nested ones alike, enumerated in 004_designated_array.c and in
004_designated_array.expected -- is rejected. No admissible gate deviation exists either: the gate's
removable members are exactly -pedantic, for the GCC-extensions area, and -Wconversion with
-Wsign-conversion, for the deliberate narrowing program, so -Wextra is not removable and area 03 is
granted no deviation at all. 004_designated_array therefore brackets its five overriding declarations
with matched push/pop diagnostic-control directives that suppress -Woverride-init for those
declarations alone, claims no gate deviation, and keeps -Werror and -Woverride-init fatal everywhere
else in its translation unit -- verified by measurement, since an override written outside those
regions is still rejected. Concentrating that mechanism in ONE program of the area is the point of
the division: this program remains entirely free of diagnostic-control directives, so the interaction
of mixed positional and designated initializers with brace elision, -Wmissing-braces and
-Wmissing-field-initializers is demonstrated on source that needs no suppression at all, and a
divergence here can never be confused with an artefact of a suppressed diagnostic.

An override carrying a SIDE EFFECT is excluded from the area altogether, and that exclusion is not
about the gate: -Woverride-init-side-effects is on by default and is not a gate member at all, and
C11 6.7.9p23 leaves the sequencing of an initializer list's side effects unspecified, which
requirement 1 forbids outright. Every override the area carries is a constant expression, so the
exclusion costs it nothing. Constraint C3 is satisfied the way it asks to be: the exclusion is
narrow, it is scoped to one spelling, it changes no target, no optimization level and no oracle, and
its reason is recorded here and in the affected program's own header comment.

THREE GATE FACTS GOVERN THE SHAPE OF THESE INITIALIZERS and must not be disturbed by anyone editing
the program. First, -Wextra enables -Wmissing-field-initializers, which in C does not fire for a
designated initializer but does for a positional partial one, so every struct here that omits a
member omits it via a designator and every fully positional struct initializer supplies all of its
members; removing a designator would trip the gate. Second, -Wall enables -Wmissing-braces, so
every nested aggregate here is fully braced; eliding a brace would trip the gate as well. Third,
-Wextra enables -Woverride-init, so no initializer here may name a subobject an earlier one already
named -- which is why the overlapping spelling is carried by 004_designated_array instead, as set out
above. All three are honoured in THIS program by writing gate-clean source rather than by suppressing
a diagnostic, and this translation unit contains no diagnostic-suppression directive of any kind.
Two neighbouring programs make the same choice for the first two, so the shape of these three
constraints across the area is a coherent division rather than three accidents:
003_partial_zero_fill.c excludes the positional partial STRUCT spelling and 002_nested_aggregate.c
excludes the brace-elided spelling, each recording its own reason in its own header and its own
record, while the overlapping-designator spelling is neither excluded nor spread across the area but
concentrated in 004_designated_array.c, whose record states the mechanism and its verified scope.

WHAT REMAINS UNDER TEST IS THE HARDER HALF OF THE SAME QUESTION -- tracking the current object
through a descent -- which is why leaving the overlapping spelling to a sibling program costs this
program nothing and is a division of labour rather than a retreat from the area's mandate. Form 1 lands a value positionally, descends into a brace where a designator sets q and
leaves p zero, then resumes positionally on trailer. Form 2 designates tag, then an UNLABELLED
brace that must bind to the following member, then a bare value that must continue past it. Form 3
takes a positional element then a designated one, skipping the element between. Form 4 fills row 0
positionally and then jumps straight to [2][1], leaving five elements zero. Form 5 nests form 1 one
level deeper beside a designated sibling array. Form 6 spells `.o = { .in.p = 42 }` -- two levels
down, leaving o.tag, o.in.q and o.trailer zero -- alongside `.pr = { { 43, 44 }, [1].q = 46 }`, a
positional element followed by a combined index-and-member designator. None of them names a slot
twice, which is exactly why all six are gate-clean.

Forms 1, 3 and 5 are repeated at automatic storage duration, so the static-image path and the
run-time path are both exercised; form 3's twin uses the combined [2].q spelling rather than
[2] = { ... }. That pairing is the discriminating variant in this area and is why all three
optimization levels matter: with optimization off the statics appear as data-section bytes while
the twins appear as a run of stores into the frame, and at a higher level either path may be folded
into immediate operands. A volatile operand would add nothing, because the subject here is what an
initializer produces rather than what an operator computes.

TWO LINE GROUPS CARRY DISPROPORTIONATE DIAGNOSTIC VALUE, and a reviewer reading a divergence should
look at them first. g_deep_desig is the most demanding initializer in area 03: it requires the
compiler to descend two nesting levels through .o.in.p, zero everything else in o, and then handle
a positional array element followed by a combined index-and-member designator [1].q in the sibling
array member; nearly every plausible current-object defect surfaces in its eight lines.
g_m_pos_then_desig is the clearest single-line detector: after a positional row 0, the designator
[2][1] = 8 must place a single 8 while row 1 and five of row 2's six elements stay zero, so a
designator landing in the wrong row or column is immediately visible.

WIDTH NORMALIZATION. Every member is an int and %d is the only conversion specifier, so no target's
pointer or long width can be observed: i686 is ELF32 with a four-byte long and pointer while
x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 are ELF64 with eight bytes for both, and this program touches neither
type. It contains no long, size_t, ptrdiff_t, intptr_t, float, double or long double. No sizeof or
_Alignof result is printed and no address is printed, so no layout choice the ABI is free to make
is observable.

PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS. The only character data is the format-string literals, whose bytes printf
copies through unchanged; no plain-char value is read as a number, converted, compared or formatted
numerically, so the MEASURED split -- signed on x86-64 and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64 --
cannot arise.

PADDING. Every member at every nesting level is read individually by name; no aggregate is printed
whole and no representation is inspected, so no padding byte is ever observed.

EXECUTION CHARACTER SET. Nothing character-valued is printed, so C11 5.2.1 leaves nothing here to
the implementation.

MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 57 lines byte-identically with
exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other without
any narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. These 57 lines are the
output of the source committed beside this record. Nothing is summarized, so one
divergent line localizes the defect to one mixed form at one nesting level.
END

